    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA charming four-bedroom detached dormer bungalow ideally positioned within a small private enclave in the sought-after development of Monks Glade. Offering spacious and well-proportioned accommodation throughout, this property presents an excellent opportunity for buyers seeking a family home in a peaceful coastal setting with scope to modernise and add value.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises a bright living room, kitchen, four bedrooms, and a main family bathroom. Outside, the property enjoys gardens to the front and rear together with secure parking.\n\nWhile the property would benefit from some upgrading and modernisation, it offers tremendous potential to create a superb home tailored to individual tastes and requirements. Conveniently located close to the coastline and within easy reach of Blainroe, this home combines privacy, space, and excellent potential in a highly desirable location.\n\nResidents of Blainroe Estate may apply for membership of Blainroe Golf Club without additional qualifications, although standard membership rates apply. Estate amenities include tennis courts, a pavilion for social events, a football pitch, and private beach access with summer monitoring. A padel court is also available for residents, subject to a usage charge.\n\nLocated in the heart of Blainroe, this property enjoys a peaceful coastal setting in one of Wicklow's most desirable residential areas. Blainroe is renowned for its scenic surroundings, beautiful coastline, and relaxed village atmosphere while remaining conveniently close to a range of amenities.\n\nThe area offers easy access to beaches, coastal walks, and the well-known Blainroe Golf Club, making it an ideal location for outdoor enthusiasts and families alike. Nearby Wicklow Town provides an excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants, schools, and transport links, while the N11/M11 offers convenient access to Dublin and surrounding areas.\n\nCombining coastal charm with everyday convenience, Blainroe offers an exceptional lifestyle in a tranquil yet accessible setting."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 4.60m x 1.97m\nLight filled entrance hallway with durable tiled flooring underfoot and an open stairwell giving access to the first floor.\n\nLiving Room - 5.56m x 3.73m\nThis living room enjoys a dual aspect allowing plenty of natural light flood the room. Overlooking the garden it has a pleasant outlook and there is a wood burning stove for those cosy nights spent indoors. tiled floors complete this room.\n\nKitchen - 2.45m x 1.86m\nA compact kitchen located to the rear of the house with a range of storage units and countertop space for food prep. For the enthusiastic cheh there is an electric oven, a sink unit with tiled splashback also features. Finally there is plumbing in place for a washer/dryer, tiled flooring underfoot and access to the rear garden.\n\nShower Room - 1.97m x 1.86m\nLocated on the ground floor and featuring tiled flooring, shower unit, wc and whb.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.81m x 2.27m\nDouble bedroom located on the ground floor to the rear with carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.70m x 2.27m\nSingle bedroom to the front with tiled flooring underfoot.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.75m x 3.61m\nSpacious double bedroom located on the first floor with carpet flooring underfoot and eaves storage.\n\nEn-Suite - 2.32m x 1.13m\nFeaturing shower, wc and whb.\n\nEaves - 4.71m x 1.86m\nAttic storage.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.65m x 3.40m\nDouble bedroom with carpet flooring underfoot and walk in wardrobe.\n\n"
      },
      {
